{"name":"Catlinite","hex":"#9e4d28","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"catlinite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brownish-red red clay found in Northern USA and Canada, used by the American Indians to make pipes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catlinite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Catlinite","blocks":[{"text":"Catlinite, also called pipestone, is a type of argillite, usually brownish-red in color, which occurs in a matrix of Sioux Quartzite. Because it is fine-grained and easily worked, it is prized by Native Americans, primarily those of the Plains nations, for use in making ceremonial pipes, known as chanunpas. Pipestone quarries are located and preserved in Pipestone National Monument outside Pipestone, Minnesota, in Pipestone County, Minnesota, and at the Pipestone River in Ontario, Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/WLA_brooklynmuseum_Native_American_Plains_Pipe_Bowl_representing_Owl.jpg/330px-WLA_brooklynmuseum_Native_American_Plains_Pipe_Bowl_representing_Owl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catlinite","wikidata":"Q931082"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Iowa_catlinite_pipe_wanampito.jpg/500px-Iowa_catlinite_pipe_wanampito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Iowa_catlinite_pipe_wanampito.jpg/500px-Iowa_catlinite_pipe_wanampito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Protohistoric Catlinite pipe, probably late 17th century Ioway, from the Wanampito site in Iowa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIowa_catlinite_pipe_wanampito.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Black_hawk_calumet.jpg/500px-Black_hawk_calumet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai